# Walkthrough: Client-Side PDF Generation & Atomic Storage Sync

We have completed the implementation of the **Client-Side PDF Generation Pipeline** using `@react-pdf/renderer` with on-demand code splitting and atomic Supabase storage sync.

---

## Changes Implemented

### 1. Dedicated PDF Report Generator ([`src/services/pdfReport.jsx`](file:///c:/property_pwa/src/services/pdfReport.jsx))
* Built a branded A4 PDF document template using `@react-pdf/renderer`.
* **Header:** InspectPWA branding, Estate Name, Unit Number, Inspector, and Date.
* **Executive Summary:** Quick-reference count grid for Total Defects, Critical (Red), Moderate (Amber), and Minor (Blue).
* **Deficiencies Punch-List:** Dynamic mapping with `wrap={false}` on cards to ensure clean multi-page pagination without awkward card splits.
* **Photo References:** Clickable links (`<Link src={photoUrl}>`) directly to high-res inspection photos in Supabase Storage.
* **Export Helper:** `generateInspectionPdfBlob(data)` to compile binary `application/pdf` blobs in-memory.

### 2. Submission Pipeline & Storage Sync ([`src/services/submission.js`](file:///c:/property_pwa/src/services/submission.js))
* **Photo Uploads:** Uploaded to `/photos/{YYYY-MM}/{id}/{photo_id}.webp`.
* **Dynamic Code-Splitting:** Dynamically loads the PDF engine (`await import('./pdfReport.jsx')`) on submission.
* **PDF Upload:** Generates and uploads PDF blob to `/reports/{YYYY-MM}/{id}.pdf` with `contentType: 'application/pdf'`.
* **Atomic PostgreSQL Insert:** Inserts row into `property_inspections` with `pdf_url` populated on row #1.

### 3. User Interface Enhancements ([`src/App.jsx`](file:///c:/property_pwa/src/App.jsx) & [`src/components/SyncBanner.jsx`](file:///c:/property_pwa/src/components/SyncBanner.jsx))
* **Success Modal:** Prominently displays a **"📄 View / Download PDF Report"** button to open the live generated PDF in a new tab.
* **Version Bump:** Bumped to **`v1.0.5` (Cache: `v5`)** across the UI badge, bottom footer, Service Worker, and `index.html`.

